[146.571234, "o", "# refund-webhooks\r\n\r\nReceives Paygate refund webhooks and exposes a small internal refunds API used by the\r\npayments ops console and finance analytics.\r\n\r\n| Path | What |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `src/server.ts` | HTTP routes (`npm start`, `PORT`, `DATA_DIR`, `CONFIG_DIR`) |\r\n| `src/verify.ts` | `Paygate-Signature` parsing and verification |\r\n| `src/refunds.ts` | event parsing, refund policy, event processing |\r\n| `src/store.ts` | file-backed state (`data/state.json`), raw events, audit log |\r\n| `src/authz.ts` | bearer-key auth and role permissions (`config/roles.json`) |\r\n| `config/` | roles, refund policy, Paygate signing secrets and freshness window (`paygate.json`: `tolerance_s`, for both normal and replay deliveries) |\r\n| `docs/SPEC.md` | webhook contract and API |\r\n| `ops/HANDOFF.md` | on-call handoff notes |\r\n\r\nRuns on Node 22 with type stripping, no dependencies.\r\n\r\n    npm test\r\n    npm start\r\n\r\nPaygate replays must supply a fresh `X-Replay-Timestamp` and valid `X-Replay-Signature`.\r\nLegacy `replay_tolerance_s` / `PAYGATE_REPLAY_TOLERANCE_S` settings do not widen the\r\nauthentication window; the original delivery signature is not used for replays.\r\n"]
[146.572778, "o", "import assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\r\nimport { mkdtempSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, rmSync } from \"node:fs\";\r\nimport { createServer } from \"node:http\";\r\nimport type { AddressInfo } from \"node:net\";\r\nimport { tmpdir } from \"node:os\";\r\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\r\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\r\nimport { decideStatus, parseEvent, processEvent } from \"../src/refunds.ts\";\r\nimport { buildApp } from \"../src/server.ts\";\r\nimport { Store } from \"../src/store.ts\";\r\nimport { computeSignature, SignatureError, verifyReplay, verifyWebhook } from \"../src/verify.ts\";\r\n\r\nconst SECRET = \"whsec_regression\";\r\nconst POLICY = { auto_approve_max_minor: 500_000, auto_approve_currencies: [\"INR\"] };\r\n"]
